WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:02.070
SPEAKER 1: Ready for a challenge?

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.880
Here is another example.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.510
It's a real case, too, though I am adapting the details

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:14.160
for when this occurred in the 1800's just to get the money up

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.050
to today's standards.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:21.470
We have a rich uncle, who is very fond of his nephew.

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:24.710
But his nephew, he thinks-- a young man.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.720
He's late adolescent.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:32.850
He kind of runs in bad company, and he needs to get his act together.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:39.520
So what he says, look, I'll give you a quarter of a million dollars

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:46.080
when you reach the age of 21 on condition that in the next few years,

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:53.300
before you are 21, you don't drink, you don't smoke, you don't swear,

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:57.510
and you don't gamble.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:02.520
Well, the nephew keeps to these terms all that time.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:07.130
He doesn't smoke, drink, gamble.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:10.580
And come 21, he wants his money.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:16.160
Now, may I say in the meanwhile, the good hearted uncle had died.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:22.280
And who the nephew was suing for the money are his lawyers and his heirs.

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.570
And though the uncle may have been minded to give the money,

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:30.400
the lawyers are more hard hearted and they say,

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.780
we're not going to give you this money.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:33.820
Why?

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:42.130
Because it was simply a promise to make a gift and our law does not enforce

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:45.250
promises to make gifts.

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:49.320
So if you want to make a gift, make your gift.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.160
Once you make your gift, or you hand over the quarter of a million dollars

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:58.570
or you hand over the silver watch or you hand over the house, well that's fine.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:01:59.800
You've transferred it.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.190
Now, it belongs to the other person.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:06.290
But a promise to make a gift, we're not going to bother with.

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:08.550
You can't take that to court.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:11.870
Well, do you know what happened in this case?

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:13.940
Do you know who won?

